  <h2 id="capability-leases">Capability Leases</h2>

  <p>
    Cloudflare gets provisioned capabilities, not raw substrate access. The
    trusted relay owns local paths, Typesense/docs credentials, transcript
    hydration, comms credentials, org policy, redaction, source-specific
    backfills, and artifact capture. Cloudflare receives redacted evidence,
    hashes, coverage counts, freshness, trace ids, lease receipts, and links it
    is allowed to follow.
  </p>

  <h2 id="t-shaped-dreaming">T-Shaped Dreaming</h2>

  <p>
    Wide means explicit horizons: last 24h, 7d, 30d, quarter, and all-time
    across Pi, Codex, Claude, Cloudflare, Brain, docs, repos, reports, and comms.
    Deep means selected evidence gets hydrated, correlated, and checked against
    older memory, repeated corrections, package manifests, accepted Brain claims,
    prior reports, runtime outputs, and unresolved promises.
  </p>

  <h2 id="kernel-loop">Kernel And Package Loop</h2>

  <p>
    The output is not a vibes report. Dreams propose concrete refinements:
    kernel memories, package boundaries, workflow-node plugins, access leases,
    schema/types, observability requirements, report-node improvements, and
    generated workflow patterns. Accepted dreams leave receipts and update the
    next workflow so the system gets smarter instead of merely louder.
  </p>

  <h2 id="generated-proof">Proof Contract</h2>

